# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# There is deliberately NO `/*  /index.html  200` catch-all. Every public route
# is prerendered to its own dist/<route>/index.html (see PRERENDER_ROUTES in
# src/entry-server.tsx), so Pages serves those as real files and deep links work
# without a fallback. A catch-all would additionally serve the homepage — with a
# 200 — for every URL that does NOT exist, which is a soft 404: Googlebot sees
# success, Search Console fills with "Soft 404", and genuinely dead URLs can
# never signal that they're gone. Unmatched paths now fall through to 404.html
# with a real 404 status.
#
# So: any new route MUST be added to PRERENDER_ROUTES, or it will 404 in
# production even though it works in dev. That includes private/app-like routes
# — prerender them and keep them out of search with noindex, as /admin does.
/api/*  /api/:splat  200

# Retired URLs → 301 to a live page. These must come BEFORE the /* catch-all
# (Cloudflare matches top-down, first hit wins); otherwise the catch-all would
# serve the homepage at 200 and the old URL would linger as a soft-404 in Search
# Console. /getstarted was an old "get started" CTA that 404'd (GSC: Not found,
# last crawled Apr 2026) — send it home so Google retires it cleanly. Repoint to
# /signup or /how-it-works/ instead if that's where it should land.
/getstarted   /  301
/getstarted/  /  301

# NOTE: /admin needs no rule here. It's prerendered like every other route (see
# PRERENDER_ROUTES), so Pages serves dist/admin/index.html directly. Rewriting it
# to /index.html does NOT work — Pages canonicalises /index.html to / and turns
# the 200 rewrite into a 308 to the homepage. Verified with `wrangler pages dev`.
